From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 09 Oct 2026 15:56:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bring-up tooling: run statistics, call trace, scripted pad,
 debug rasteriser

For the first headless run of a new game under the interpreter, with no
window, no renderer and no GPU. Every switch is off unless its environment
variable is set, and none changes what the guest sees except where noted.

* host/perf/bringup_stats.*: <prefix>_STATS=<dir> writes per-flip and
  per-phase CSVs (instructions, HLE calls, lists, draws), calls per import
  and thread, per-address instruction counts, and a GE aggregate (vertex
  types, texture formats, blends, depth/alpha functions, lights, render
  targets, command histogram). _MAX_FRAMES/_MAX_WALL/_MAX_EMU stop a run
  cleanly so the end-of-run report prints; _PAD_SCRIPT drives the pad by flip
  or emulated time; _TRACE_CALLS (and _TRACE_FROM_FLIP) prints the first N
  calls to matching imports, with file names for sceIoOpen.
* host/perf/debug_raster.*: a small software rasteriser behind
  <prefix>_SHOT_DIR/_SHOT_FLIPS/_SHOT_EVERY that writes the displayed frame as
  a PNG, so a headless run can be looked at and a menu navigated. Not a
  renderer: no lighting or fog, nearest sampling, nothing written back.
* interpreter: per-address instruction counts (set_interpreter_pc_profile)
  and interpreter_account_native() so a native replacement of a guest
  function keeps instruction counts and profiles comparable.
* runtime: set_runtime_pre_import_hook(), called before every import.
* GeState: per-opcode command counters.
* kernel: <prefix>_CPU_NS_PER_INSN charges emulated time per interpreted
  instruction (guest compute otherwise costs none), and
  <prefix>_FRAME_LIMIT_US keeps flips at least that far apart in emulated time.
* sceKernelReferThreadProfiler / ReferGlobalProfiler return NULL and write
  nothing (UNVERIFIED: logged as such); before, they wrote through whatever
  pointer the guest had in a0.

Verified: builds with the framework's own targets and with a port, on x86_64
Linux, without a renderer. Not verified: the renderer build (SDL3/Vulkan are
not available here), any other game, the CPU time model against hardware.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

